{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QBetaBarEvenKernelInvariant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QBetaBarEvenKernelInvariant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenInvariant.bar_even_test_n2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenInvariant.bar_even_test_n2","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant.lean#L90-L120","doc":"**The N=2 bar-even invariant test: $R(q,\\xi) - R(q^{-1},\\xi^{-1}) = 0$\non the N=2 factor.**\n\nThe bar-involution acts on the symbolic substrate by $b \\mapsto b$\n(manifestly q-symmetric: $b^2(q^{-1}) = b^2(q)$ in the ring of\nLaurent polynomials, verified symbolically in\n`qbeta_symbolic_chain_alpha_b.py`) and $\\hbar^2 \\mapsto q^2 \\cdot\n\\hbar^2$ at the FORMAL level (since $\\hbar_q(q^{-1}) = -q \\cdot\n\\hbar_q(q)$, hence $\\hbar_q^2(q^{-1}) = q^2 \\cdot \\hbar_q^2(q)$).\nThe N=2 ladder factor $1 - b^2 \\cdot \\hbar^4$ under bar then\nbecomes $1 - b^2 \\cdot q^4 \\cdot \\hbar^4$.  The DIFFERENCE\n$(1 - b^2 \\cdot \\hbar^4) - (1 - b^2 \\cdot q^4 \\cdot \\hbar^4) =\nb^2 \\cdot \\hbar^4 \\cdot (q^4 - 1)$ vanishes IFF $q^4 = 1$\n(root-of-unity case) — a formal statement matching the audit doc's\n\"fibre-level / cyclotomic\" framing.\n\nFor the substrate q in $1 < q < 1 + \\sqrt{2}$ (proton-anchor region),\nthe factor $q^4 - 1 \\neq 0$, so the N=2 ladder factor IS bar-asymmetric\nat the archimedean level — exactly the obstruction PR #1840 flagged.\nThe bar-even discriminant CORRECTLY identifies this asymmetry as the\nreason scalar c_k extraction fails: only the operator-level grading\nrecovers the c_k.\n\nEncoded here as a one-line ring identity expressing the bar-asymmetry\nmeasure: $b^2 \\cdot \\hbar^4 \\cdot (q^4 - 1)$ is the obstruction\nquantity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenInvariant.bar_even_invariant_pure_uk_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenInvariant.bar_even_invariant_pure_uk_term","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant.lean#L71-L88","doc":"**Generic even-$k$ ladder factor is bar-even at the Taylor level.**\n\nFor any coefficient $a$ and any natural $m$, the ladder factor\n$(1 + a \\cdot u^{2m})$ with $u = b \\cdot \\hbar^2$ equals\n$(1 + a \\cdot (u^m)^2)$ — only even powers of $u$ appear, so the\nTaylor expansion in $t = q - 1$ contributes only at orders\n$t^{4m}, t^{4m+1}, \\ldots$ (with the leading $t^{4m}$ term EVEN\nin $t$).\n\nThis generalises `bar_even_quadratic_term_in_t_squared` from\n$m = 1$ (the N=2 factor) to arbitrary even ladder rungs.  Proved\nby `pow_mul` on the variable exponent (`ring` does not handle\n`^(2*m)` for `m : ℕ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarEvenInvariant.bar_even_quadratic_term_in_t_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarEvenInvariant.bar_even_quadratic_term_in_t_squared","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant.lean#L55-L69","doc":"**The N=2 ladder factor expressed in u has only even powers.**\n\nSetting $u := b \\cdot \\hbar^2$, the N=2 categorical correction\nfactor $(1 - b^2 \\cdot \\hbar^4)$ is identically $(1 - u^2)$ — a\npolynomial in $u$ with only the constant and $u^2$ terms (no\n$u^1$ or $u^3$, etc.).  This is the bar-even prototype: only\nEVEN powers of $u$ appear, which under the leading-order\nTaylor expansion of $u \\sim b(1) \\cdot t^2$ at $q = 1$\ncorresponds to only even powers of $t = q - 1$.\n\nPure ring identity in any commutative ring. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant","label":"prop:q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-bar-even-kernel-invariant.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}